{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2176-08-13 23:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello Mr. ___, I'm Dr. ___. I see you came in with abdominal pain and bloating. Can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2176-08-13 23:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, doctor. For the past three days, my belly has been really distended and painful. I haven’t had a bowel movement in three days, but I am passing gas. I also feel short of breath, especially when I move."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2176-08-13 23:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you mentioned you stopped your laxatives recently because you were having frequent bowel movements in the hospital?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2176-08-13 23:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s right. I thought I didn’t need them anymore, but now I regret it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2176-08-13 23:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Understandable. We’ve reviewed your labs and imaging. Your creatinine is improving—down to 2.1 from over 5—so your kidneys are recovering from the last admission. The abdominal X-ray shows moderate fecal load, but no obstruction."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2176-08-13 23:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So is it just constipation causing all this?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2176-08-13 23:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s likely a big part of it. You passed a large bowel movement last night, and you say your pain improved?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2176-08-13 23:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it got much better after that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2176-08-13 23:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. But because your symptoms didn’t fully resolve and you couldn’t tolerate food well, we ordered a CT scan. It showed inflammation in the duodenum—your first part of the small intestine. We’re calling it duodenitis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2176-08-13 23:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Duodenitis? What causes that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2176-08-13 23:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can be from infection, medications, or even your multiple myeloma. One possibility is that your recent Velcade treatment may have contributed. We’ll need more tests to be sure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2176-08-14 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We did an MRI today to get a better look. It confirms duodenitis with significant inflammation. There’s also a mass near your bladder—likely extramedullary hematopoiesis, which can happen with myeloma."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2176-08-14 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that cancerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2176-08-14 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s not a typical cancer, but it’s abnormal blood cell production outside the bone marrow. We’ll monitor it closely. The bigger concern right now is your belly pain and distention worsening again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2176-08-14 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It started hurting again this morning, and I feel very full."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2176-08-14 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re concerned about a partial bowel obstruction. Your blood sugar also dropped to 36 this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2176-08-14 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I felt shaky and confused. They gave me orange gel and an IV."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2176-08-14 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that was D50. We’re switching you to a continuous dextrose IV to prevent more lows. Given your abdominal changes, we’re moving you to the ICU for closer monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2176-08-14 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve placed a nasogastric tube to decompress your stomach. It’s draining a lot of fluid—about 4 liters in the first 24 hours. This should help relieve the pressure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2176-08-14 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It feels a little better already. Will I need surgery?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2176-08-14 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not likely. The imaging doesn’t show a blockage or perforation. This looks like pseudo-obstruction from inflammation. We’ll keep the NG tube in for a few days and see if your gut starts working again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2176-08-15 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your NG output has decreased to less than 200 mL in the last 12 hours—that’s a good sign. We’re going to try giving you small sips of water."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2176-08-15 07:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great, I’m thirsty. What about the low blood sugar?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2176-08-15 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked your C-peptide and insulin levels. Your insulin was high but C-peptide low—this suggests you may have been getting too much insulin at home, especially with poor food intake here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2176-08-15 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was on 46 units at night because of steroids. Should I go back to that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2176-08-15 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. The endocrine team recommends holding long-acting insulin for now and using only sliding scale. We’ll restart it slowly once you’re eating regularly and off steroids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2176-08-16 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We removed the NG tube this morning. You tolerated a soft diet yesterday without vomiting or pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2176-08-16 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad that tube is out. When can I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2176-08-16 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. We still need to address your multiple myeloma. Your IgA levels are rising again, and your blood counts are dropping—this suggests relapse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2176-08-16 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the cancer is active again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2176-08-16 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’re starting you on high-dose dexamethasone for four days, followed by a Cytoxan infusion. This will help control the myeloma and may improve your blood counts."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2176-08-17 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve completed the steroid course. Your blood pressure went up to 180s, but that’s expected with steroids. It’s coming down now that we’ve stopped them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2176-08-17 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I felt a bit jittery. My sugars were high too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2176-08-17 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, they reached 500. We adjusted your insulin and will taper it as the steroids wear off. Your liver enzymes are also mildly elevated—could be from medication or hepatitis B. We’ll check your viral load."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2176-08-18 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your HBV viral load came back—no detectable virus. That’s good. We’ll keep you on lamivudine. We also did a colonoscopy to check for colon cancer, given your history with Strep bovis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2176-08-18 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2176-08-18 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No cancer found. You had some benign polyps removed. We also did an EGD—your duodenum shows inflammation, but no ulcer or mass. Biopsies are pending."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2176-08-19 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine is now 1.5—much better. Your kidney function continues to improve. We’re discharging you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2176-08-19 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What about the mass near my bladder?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2176-08-19 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We sent urine cytology—it showed atypical cells. You’ll need follow-up with urology to check it further. Could be related to the extramedullary hematopoiesis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2176-08-20 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re moving your bowels regularly and eating well. We’re planning discharge tomorrow if all goes well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2176-08-20 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been using the walker like they showed me. I feel stronger."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2176-08-20 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We restarted your CPAP for sleep apnea. You tolerated it well. You’ll need a new machine—your old provider lost their license."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2176-08-21 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—we gave you a dose of Cytoxan yesterday. Your oncologist, Dr. ___, will see you soon to discuss next steps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2176-08-21 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll call his office. What about my insulin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2176-08-21 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll go home on 16 units of Lantus at bedtime and Humalog sliding scale. Check your sugars before meals and at bedtime. If over 250, use the high-dose scale; if lower, use your usual one."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2176-08-21 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my blood pressure meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2176-08-21 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Same as before—carvedilol, diltiazem, doxazosin. Just get your pressure checked at your next appointment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2176-08-22 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set. You’re discharged. Keep all your follow-ups: oncology, urology, GI for biopsy results, and endocrinology."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2176-08-22 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. I feel much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2176-08-23 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick call to check in. How are you feeling at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2176-08-23 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. Bowels are regular, no pain. I started the vancomycin taper as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2176-08-23 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. Keep up with the laxatives and PPI for your stomach. Call if you have fever, vomiting, or severe pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2176-08-24 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your EGD biopsies came back—no infection or malignancy, just chronic inflammation. Continue the pantoprazole."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2176-08-24 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Any update on the bladder mass?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2176-08-24 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Urology has scheduled you for a cystoscopy. We’ll get more answers soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2176-08-25 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your liver enzymes are stable. No need for further action now. Keep monitoring them at your next visit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2176-08-26 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your hemoglobin is stable at 7.5. No transfusion needed. Continue B12 and folate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2176-08-27 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming—you took the single dose of furosemide on the day we discussed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2176-08-27 13:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I did. Felt a bit more urination that day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2176-08-27 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. That was just to help with any fluid retention from the steroids. No need to continue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2176-08-28 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your platelets are improving—up to 43,000. That’s a good sign your bone marrow is recovering."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2176-08-28 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t had any more nosebleeds or bruising."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2176-08-28 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Keep using the nasal saline to prevent dryness from CPAP."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2176-08-29 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last call. Make sure you schedule your repeat colonoscopy in one year, as recommended."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2176-08-29 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I already called. They said six months might be better given my history."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2176-08-29 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s fine. Just stay on top of it. Otherwise, you’re doing very well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2176-08-30 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We infused your Cytoxan safely. Oncology will guide next steps. Keep up the good work."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2176-08-30 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, doctor. I’ll see Dr. ___ next week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2176-08-31 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final update: your discharge labs show stable kidney function, improved blood counts, and no infection. You’ve come a long way."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2176-08-31 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel lucky to be here. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2176-08-31 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been through a lot, but you’re on the right track. Stay in touch with your team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2176-08-31 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a reminder—your wife is listed as your contact. Make sure she has all the discharge papers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2176-08-31 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "She’s picking me up soon. She’s been amazing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2176-08-31 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. Take care, Mr. ___. We’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2176-08-31 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—your hepatitis B remains inactive. Continue lamivudine as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2176-08-31 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’ll get the CPAP sorted with my PCP."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2176-08-31 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. You’re all set for a smooth recovery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2176-08-31 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The urology appointment is confirmed for tomorrow at 1 PM. They’ll discuss the next steps for the perivesicular mass."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2176-08-31 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll be there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2176-08-31 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your GI follow-up is scheduled for next week to review the biopsy results in detail."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2176-08-31 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make sure to ask about the duodenitis treatment plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2176-08-31 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, they’ll likely continue the PPI and monitor for symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2176-08-31 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final check before discharge: any last questions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2176-08-31 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think we’ve covered everything. Thank you for your care."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2176-08-13 23:29:00",
    "admission_end": "2176-08-31 16:36:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. ___ was admitted with severe abdominal pain, distention, and constipation three days after discharge from a prior admission for cast nephropathy in the setting of relapsed multiple myeloma. Initial evaluation revealed moderate fecal load and improving renal function with a creatinine of 2.1. He developed worsening abdominal distention and pain with guarding, leading to ICU transfer and NG tube placement for decompression due to partial bowel obstruction. Imaging confirmed duodenitis and a perivesicular mass likely representing extramedullary hematopoiesis. He experienced hypoglycemia attributed to insulin stacking and CKD, managed with D10W and insulin regimen adjustment. After stabilization, he received a four-day course of dexamethasone and Cytoxan for relapsed myeloma, underwent EGD and colonoscopy showing non-specific duodenitis and no malignancy, and completed a vancomycin taper for C. diff. His symptoms resolved, renal function improved to a creatinine of 1.5, and he was discharged home on insulin, PPI, and scheduled follow-ups with oncology, urology, and GI.",
    "problems": [
      "Duodenitis without bleeding",
      "Multiple myeloma in relapse",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Enterocolitis due to Clostridium difficile",
      "Unspecified intestinal obstruction",
      "Constipation, unspecified",
      "Chronic viral hepatitis B without delta-agent",
      "Type 2 diabetes mellitus with hypoglycemia without coma",
      "Long term (current) use of insulin",
      "Obstructive sleep apnea (adult) (pediatric)",
      "Anemia, unspecified",
      "Transaminitis of unclear etiology",
      "Perivesicular mass",
      "Hypertensive chronic kidney disease with stage 1 through stage 4 chronic kidney disease, or unspecified chronic kidney disease"
    ]
  }
}
